    {
      "turn": 2,
      "doctor_question": "What has been bothering you the most lately?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S002",
      "patient_response": "I mean, what’s bothering me most is that I just can't keep my mind on a task long enough to finish it anymore. And it's not just the little things, it's the important stuff, the things I really need to get done for work. I’m a computer support specialist, right? So a lot of my job is figuring out why things aren't working. I'll get a ticket, a client's network is down or lagging or whatever, and I'll start tracing the problem. I pull up the logs, I'm looking at the data, I'm ready to figure it out. And then... I don't even know what happens. Ten minutes later, I realize I've just been staring at the screen. I'll have reread the exact same block of log entries, like, three times, and I still don't know what they actually say. It's like my brain just slides right off the information. I look at the words, the numbers, the IP addresses, and it's just noise. And then I have to start all over again, and by then I'm frustrated, and I'm worried the client is getting impatient, and... it's just exhausting. It takes me three times as long to do something that should be straightforward, just because I can't keep my focus locked in.",
