    {
      "turn": 4,
      "doctor_question": "Have you been feeling down or depressed lately?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "Down or depressed? No, I wouldn't say that. I mean, sure, I get frustrated, like I was saying about the logs and the tickets and feeling like I'm letting people down because I can't just do the thing I'm supposed to do. That definitely gets me down in the moment, you know? It's discouraging when you know you're smart enough to do the job—I have a master's degree, for crying out loud, I know how networks operate—but your brain just won't cooperate. But it's not like a dark cloud hanging over my whole life, if that's what you mean. I still enjoy things when I'm not working, I still like hanging out with my friends, I still like tinkering with my own computers at home... well, when I can actually finish a project, anyway. But no, I don't wake up feeling sad or hopeless or anything like that. It's really just this constant, overwhelming frustration with myself and my inability to just focus. It's like my engine is running, but the transmission keeps slipping out of gear. So, depressed? No. Just incredibly, incredibly annoyed with my own brain.",
